# AERIS Phase 5 safety params: PX4's own S0 geofence backstop (spec §16.2).
#
# Format: see sitl_base.params's header comment (same parser,
# aeris.simulation.launcher.params.parse_params_file). Apply together with
# sitl_base.params (merge both dicts before launcher.start(..., params=...))
# -- this file is additive, not a replacement.
#
# PX4's own defaults (src/modules/navigator/geofence_params.c, read from
# the pinned checkout in Phase 5) leave GF_MAX_HOR_DIST/GF_MAX_VER_DIST at
# 0.0, which PX4 treats as "disabled" -- there is no S0 fence at all out of
# the box. These values enable it as a real backstop, deliberately larger
# than aeris.safety's own S1 envelope (configs/vehicle/safety.yaml's
# geofence_radius_m=30/altitude_ceiling_m=20) so AERIS's own validator
# trips first in normal operation; PX4's fence should only ever engage if
# AERIS's own S1/S2 layers have already failed.
#
# GF_ACTION is left at PX4's own default (2, "Hold mode") -- not overridden
# here, since it's already the right choice for a backstop.
GF_MAX_HOR_DIST 60.0
GF_MAX_VER_DIST 40.0
